## Conventions

Follow repo build/test/format/architecture patterns. Keep changes scoped and
shared contracts synchronized. Never expose secrets.

## TokenLighten Tool Gating

docs, config, logs;Office/archives/code.

- Unknown: `read_file mode=task_pack query=<complete verbatim request>`; never truncate; `taskProfile` only when user-declared, otherwise omit. Known: `read_file mode=overview|symbol|pack` or `read_file mode=small_file content=outline`; avoid `path`+`paths`.
- `execution_contract`: `readiness_certificate`+`typestate:prepared`+closed `semantic_closure`=>`evidence_model`; `discovery_allowed:true`=>`next_call` only; awaiting-input=>choose served candidate if safe, else ask. `workspace_state` binds; `pack_unchanged` revalidates. Open=>`capability_gaps[].next_call`.
- Search: `search_files action=find query=<token>`.
- Archives: `read_file mode=archive|task_pack`; virtual `outer.ext!/member` immutable; non-ZIP read-only.
- Edit: `edit_file handle=<id> allowPathFallback=false`; batch `edits[]`; tests ≤3 candidates; create `create:true content=...`/`from=<src>`; repeat `target=all`.

## Validation receipts

- Credentials: opaque `credentialRef`/`outputCredentialRef` only, never passwords; server resolves `TOKENLIGHTEN_PASSWORD_<REF>`.
- Challenge revokes epoch cert; no replay; `answer_resolution` beats decoys.
- Artifact paths need matching `artifact_sections`; create only `create_target.path`.
- With `--allow-write`, edit outer ZIP only via `edit_file artifact={kind:"zip",members:[...]}`; tar/tar.gz/7z/rar remain read-only.
- Edits validate identity, match/range/overlap, syntax, and scope. `committed` needs no confirmation read; not-written/rolled-back means no write; inspect `workspace-state-unknown` before retry.
- Re-slice handles, never paths. Candidate packs: no broad/full reads; use served bodies or one `next_call`. `downgraded_from` was served.
- Use `closure` only if an edit opened checks; otherwise diff/tests.
